{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - In light of the numerous conflicts with Development Plan policies, the proposal would fail to comply with Local Plan policy SC1 as it proposes the formation of a self-contained residential unit within the curtilage of existing dwellings while conflicting with other policies. ",
    "Reason : 2 - Owing to its excessive scale and bulk, inappropriate siting and design, failure to preserve the established visual symmetry between no.2 and its neighbour no.63 Burns Way and spacious character of the area, and its awkward relationship with the host property and the street character, the proposal would cause significant harm to the character and appearance of the area. It would also disrupt the pattern of development along the street and would represent an overdevelopment of the site. The proposal would therefore conflict with Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2. ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development would cause harm to neighbouring living conditions through the reduction in usable amenity space, the reduction in habitable internal accommodation, and the loss of outlook and light and increased sense of enclosure arising from the boundary treatment which would be erected within the rear garden. The proposal would therefore conflict with Local Plan policies CC2 and SC5.",
    "Reason : 4 - The development has failed to demonstrate that energy consumption and carbon emission reductions have been maximised onsite as far as possible through use of viable sustainability proposals and has failed to commit to offset remaining emissions through a cash in-lieu carbon offset contribution. The proposal would therefore be contrary to London Plan policies SI2 and SI15, Local Plan policies EQ1 and EQ2 and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
